0 Views•Jun 18, 2025•Knowledge--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLibrary (https://help.audible.com/s/topic/0TO4z000000SoJCGA0/library?language=en_US)\nciteturn766search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * Manage your Lists ...   * Manage your Wish List\n\n# Library\n\nLearn how to manage your Library's features and resolve any technical issues with refreshing.\n\n  * Manage your Library\n\n656236 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage your Lists\n\n66459 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage your Wish List\n\n39129 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * View accompanying PDF\n\n352580 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Use Page Sync\n\n8024 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * View your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app\n\n13095 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage Family Library Sharing\n\n1076026 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage your Lists (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-collections?language=en_US)\nciteturn766search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; ## Manage your Lists ... Give your list a name and description. ... Browse to find and select a public collection that interest you.\n\n## Manage your Lists\n\nYou'll find two types of lists in the Audible experience — personal ones you can create in your own Library and public ones curated by your favorite authors, narrators, and Audible editors. You can save these public lists to your Library from both the desktop website and app to make them easier to access and enjoy.\n\nIf you're looking for more information about your Library, please visit Manage your Library.\n\nNote: The mobile website doesn't currently support creating personal lists.\n\n## How do I create a personal list?\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Select New Lists.\n  5. Give your list a name and description.\n  6. Select Create.\n\nYou can start adding titles from your Library right away.\n\nOn the Audible website\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select Library in the site's navigation.\n  3. Select Collections.\n  4. Select New Collection.\n  5. Give your collection a name and description.\n  6. Select Create.\n\nYou can start adding titles from your Library right away.\n\n## How do I add titles to a list?\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Find the title you want to add.\n  4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\n  5. Select Add to list.\n  6. Choose the list to which you want to add the title.\n\nOn the Audible website\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Find the title you want to add.\n  4. Select + Add to… under the title.\n  5. Choose the collection you want to add the title to.\n\n\n## How do I remove a title from a list?\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Find the list that has the title.\n  5. Find the title on the list.\n  6. Select the 3-dot More menu.\n  7. Select Remove from List.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Go to your Library.\n  3. Select Collections.\n  4. Find the list that has the title.\n  5. Find the title on the list.\n  6. Select Remove from collection.\n\n## How do I remove a list?\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Go to your Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Find the list you want to remove.\n  5. Select the 3-dot More menu.\n  6. Select Remove from Lists.\n\nOn the Audible website\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Select Collections.\n  4. Find the list you want to remove.\n  5. Select Delete collection.\n  6. Confirm deletion.\n\nNote: Once deleted, lists cannot be restored, and the list will need to be created again and the titles added manually.\n\n## How do I follow public Collections?\n\nYou can listen to curated content by authors, narrators, podcast hosts and Audible editors by following these steps.\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Browse to find and select a public collection that interest you.\n  3. Select Save to Collections.\n  4. The collection will appear in your Library under Lists.\n\nNote: You can unfollow a public collection at any time by selecting your Library, Lists, then select Delete collection.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLists (https://help.audible.com/s/topic/0TO4z000000SoJ3GAK/lists?language=en_US)\nciteturn766search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;   * Manage your Lists\n\n# Lists\n\n## \n\nGet tips on saving curated lists to your Library and creating your very own personal Collections.\n\n  * Manage your Library\n\n648703 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage your Lists\n\n65414 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge\n\nNo articles found\n\n## Need more help?\n\nContact us--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListening | Audible Help (https://help.audible.com/s/listening?language=en_US)\nciteturn766search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;   * Manage your Wish List ...   * Manage your Lists\n\n# Listening\n\nExplore essential tips for listening across all devices, making the most out of your personal Library, using the player, and making your opinion about specific titles known.\n\n## Ways to listen\n\n  * Audible App Download Discontinued on Windows 11\n\n121988 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Listen with Apple Watch\n\n126008 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Listen with Alexa\n\n319397 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Listen to audiobooks with Amazon Music Unlimited\n\n292115 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Listen in Dolby Atmos\n\n110581 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Learn about Read & Listen\n\n609617 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Learn about immersion reading\n\n1506 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Discover new audi