ng PDF\n\n353598 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Use Page Sync\n\n8269 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * View your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app\n\n13236 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage Family Library Sharing\n\n1081625 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Download titles\n\n443248 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Discover new audiobooks with Maven\n\n5482 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen in the car (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-in-the-car?language=en_US)\nciteturn766view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-in-the-car?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 262\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Android Auto Apple CarPlay Ask A Question+5\nL13: ## Listen in the car\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 24, 2025\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen in the car\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-in-the-car\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Audible is compatible with Android Auto, Android Automotive Operating System, Apple CarPlay, and the Waze app. You can also use Car Mode in the Audible app for a simplified listening experience.\nL29: \nL30: Tip: To listen in your car, make sure you're connected to a network to stream titles, or download titles to your Library ahead of time for offline listening.\nL31: Safety warning: Do not interact with this app while driving. Use this app only when allowed by law and applicable traffic rules and when it is safe to do so. Using the Audible app while driving is dangerous and may result in serious injury, death, or property damage.\nL32: \nL33: In this article:\nL34:   * 【1†How do I connect to my car with Bluetooth, USB, or AUX?】\nL35:   * 【2†How do I listen with Android Auto or Apple CarPlay?】\nL36:   * 【3†How do I listen with Android Automotive Operating System?】\nL37:   * 【4†How do I listen in Car Mode?】\nL38:   * 【5†How do I listen with Waze?】\nL39:   * 【6†How do I listen in my Tesla?】\nL40:   * 【7†How do I listen in my Mercedes-Benz?】\nL41: ## How do I connect to my car with Bluetooth, USB, or AUX?\nL42: \nL43: You can listen with the Audible app in your car over Bluetooth, USB, or AUX.\nL44: \nL45: Connect via Bluetooth\nL46: \nL47: You can listen to the Audible app with Car Mode over Bluetooth. After pairing your device for the first time, it will automatically connect to your car in the future.\nL48:   1. In your device Settings, turn Bluetooth on and set your device to \"discoverable.\"\nL49:   2. Activate your car's Bluetooth. These steps may vary depending on your car's system.\nL50:   3. Pair your device with your car. You may be prompted to enter a code.\nL51: \nL52: Connect via USB cable\nL53: \nL54: You must have a USB port built-in directly to your vehicle's sound system to connect this way.\nL55: \nL56:   1. Check for a USB port in your car.\nL57:   2. Connect your phone with a USB cable.\nL58: \nL59: Connect via AUX cable\nL60: An AUX cable is different from a USB cable. It plugs directly into your radio or car with a headphone jack. You won't be able to use Apple CarPlay or Android Auto with this connection, but you can play titles directly from the Audible app on your phone with the option to use Car Mode.\nL61: \nL62:   1. Check for an AUX port in your car.\nL63:   2. Connect your phone with an AUX cable.\nL64: ## How do I listen with Android Auto or Apple CarPlay?\nL65: \nL66: With Android Auto or Apple CarPlay, you can enjoy a simplified listening experience through your car's built-in display and stereo.\nL67: \nL68: Note: You can also use your voice to control Audible on Android Auto with Alexa. Alexa isn't available when using Apple CarPlay, but you can use Siri instead.\nL69: \nL70: Listen on your car's display\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApp keeps crashing (https://help.audible.com/s/article/app-keeps-crashing?language=en_US)\nciteturn766view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/app-keeps-crashing?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 144\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android App issues Ask A Question iOS Troubleshooting\nL13: ## App keeps crashing\nL14: \nL15:   * Aug 27, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: App keeps crashing\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: app-keeps-crashing\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: There are a few troubleshooting methods to try if the Audible app is consistently crashing (closing immediately after opening) or is slowly loading information.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31: \nL32:   * 【1†Force quit the app】\nL33:   * 【2†Update the app】\nL34:   * 【3†Clear app data and cache on Android】\nL35:   * 【4†Re-install the app】\nL36:   * 【5†Temporary fixes】\nL37: ## Force quit the app\nL38: \nL39:   1. Press the home button twice or swipe up from the bottom of your screen.\nL40:   2. Close the Audible app.\nL41:   3. Reopen the Audible app.\nL42: \nL43: If the issue continues, you may need to update or reinstall your Audible app.\nL44: ## Update the app\nL45: \nL46: Occasionally, app features and functions may stop working because the app hasn't been updated to the latest version.\nL47: \nL48: Note: An update will only display if there's an update available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\nL49: ### Update the iOS app\nL50: \nL51:   1. Open the App Store.\nL52:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL53:   3. Find and select the Audible app.\nL54:   4. Select Update.\nL55:   5. Select Open to view the latest version of the Audible app.\nL56: \nL57: Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\nL58: \nL59: ### Update the Android app\nL60: \nL61:   1. Open the Google Play Store.\nL62:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL63:   3. Select My apps & games.\nL64:   4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\nL65:   5. Select Update.\nL66: ## Clear app data and cache on Android\nL67: \nL68:   1. Go to the settings on your Android device.\nL69:   2. Select Apps.\nL70:   3. Find Audible in the list of all apps.\nL71:   4. Select Storage or Storage & cache.\nL72:   5. Select Clear Cache.\nL73:   6. Select Clear Storage and confirm.\nL74: ## Re-install the app\nL75: \nL76:   1. Delete the app from your device.\nL77:   2. Open your app store.\nL78:   3. Find the Audible app.\nL79:   4. Download the app.\nL80: \nL81: Note: Uninstalling the app will remove any downloaded titles and those marked as \"Finished.\" You may re-download these titles at any time and remark as \"Finished.\"\nL82: ## Temporary fixes\nL83: \nL84: If none of the above solves the crashing problem, you can try the following to minimize disruptions:\nL85: \nL86:   * Keeping the Audible app in the foreground when listening.\nL87:   * Not switching between apps frequently.\nL88:   * Closing all other apps when using Audible.\nL89: \nL90: Did this answer your question?\nL91: \nL92: 【6†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL93: \nL94: \nL95: \nL96: 【7†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL97: \nL98:  Back to top\nL99: \nL100: 【8†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL101: \nL102: 【9†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL103: ## Need more assistance?\nL104: \nL105: 【10†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL106: \nL107: \nL108: \nL109: How sati